## Phase-4 root corrections

- `AuthorityChainUpdateError` is a closed `Cancelled | Integrity` result for
  the sole ordered reorg consumer. Allocation retains and retries the exact
  request/command internally; effect lifecycle closure while the producer is
  live is a topology integrity fault. A future broad service error cannot
  silently terminate the reorg task.
- Resolve/Verify per-owner fairness and strict Ready priority are distinct
  documented policies. Ready is `Recovery > Proposal > Remote`, fee rate,
  absolute fee, earlier arrival and deterministic identity/version, in batches
  of at most eight; it has no aging state.
- `EntryVersion` plus move-only checked-out work is the sole compute identity.
  Retired numeric compute-lease terminology is rejected from production/public
  documentation by static checks.
- CI path roots are derived from behavior implementation/workspace/integration
  evidence. Current required roots are `tx-pool`, `chain`, `sync`, `test` and
  `verification` for both pull-request and push triggers.
- Public performance documentation contains the current UAK cost model and
  reproducible evidence rules, not obsolete checkpoint status.
- The architecture blocker was removed only after the complete phase-4 gates;
  the remaining manifest blockers are correctness acceptance and performance
  acceptance.

